  "description": "Midea M-Thermal split heat pumps (ATW) through the wired controller Modbus port: control, running parameters and parameter settings",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-15",
  "source": "M-thermal Wired Controller Operation Manual (modbus mapping), MD20U-005AW",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "M-thermal Wired Controller Operation Manual (modbus mapping), MD20U-005AW",
      "version": "Section 8, Modbus mapping table (printed pages 48 to 58 of the English part)",
      "url": "https://www.midea.com.ua/sites/default/files/downloadables-documents/pdf/operation-manual-wired-controller-wcde.pdf",
      "note": "Midea Ukraine site; multilingual manual. The same Modbus tables appear in the MD19U-004AW English edition of the manual (65 pages, sha256 763319346970be79ab4f328c3a95eacbc8c5715d0cdbfc288df76d52e2129e4b, https://www.greenspirit.ee/download4u/Midea/Midea_eng/Midea_M-Thermal_Arctic_controller_manual_b_w_en.pdf)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "c37a839d9b34a3e240a67583fe09ff2627149535ff6e5896f61820951c083a22"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU slave on the wired controller port H1/H2 (A+/B-) of the hydraulic module, 9600 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit; Modbus ASCII is not supported. The wired controller port XYE connects to the hydraulic module and H1/H2 are the Modbus ports.",
    "The slave address follows the rotary switch S3 (0 to F) on the main board of the hydraulic module: position 0 gives address 16, positions 1 to 15 give addresses 1 to 15.",
    "All registers use functions 03 (read), 06 (write single) and 10 (write multiple); the manual calls them PLC addresses 40001 and up, so they are listed as holding registers. Addresses are printed as the manual gives them (0, 1 ... , address base 0).",
    "The register meanings, units and ranges are those of the manual. Where the manual gives no unit or type: temperatures are read as signed 16-bit values in whole degrees (no scale is given) and other values as unsigned. Water flow and capacity are sent as the actual value * 100 (scale 0.01). DC bus voltage is the actual value in V.",
    "The registers 247 to 254 are reserved and return a wrong-address error; 123, 236 and 239 are not described. Register 5, 128, 129, 210 and 211 are bit maps: each bit is listed as its own entry, the whole word as the first entry. Registers 270 and 272 hold packed fields.",
    "Writing to a heat pump can damage it: check before you write.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 16,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "N",
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
